<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otago is a region in the south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s South Island, with Dunedin as its main city. It was settled from 1848 by a Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland">Church of Scotland</a> colony, and the discovery of gold at Gabriel's Gully in 1861 set off the Otago gold rush, which for a time made Dunedin the largest town in New Zealand. Its economy later rested on sheep farming, and it is home to the University of Otago, founded in 1869.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otago.jpg" alt="Otago" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peetel Derived from File:New Zealand location map.svg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otago_Region_location_in_New_Zealand.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
